==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|spýja}} (compare {{etyl|fo|-}} {{m|fo|spýggja}}, {{etyl|no|-}}, {{etyl|sv|-}} and {{etyl|da|-}} {{m|sv|spy}}), from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*spīwaną}}, whence also {{etyl|nl|-}} {{m|nl|spuwen}}, {{etyl|de|-}} {{m|de|speien}}, {{etyl|en|-}} {{m|en|spew}}, {{etyl|got|-}} {{m|got|𐍃𐍀𐌴𐌹𐍅𐌰𐌽}}. Ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{m|ine-pro|*(s)ptyēw-||to spit, vomit}}. Non-Germanic cognates include {{etyl|xcl|-}} {{m|xcl|թուք}}, {{etyl|fa|-}} {{m|fa|تف||spittle}}, {{etyl|os|-}} {{m|os|ту||spittle}}, {{etyl|grc|-}} {{m|grc|πτύω||I spit out}}, {{etyl|la|-}} {{m|la|spuo}}, {{etyl|cu|-}} {{m|cu|пльвати}} ({{etyl|ru|-}} {{m|ru|плевать}}) and {{etyl|sa|-}} {{m|sa|ष्ठीवति|tr=ṣṭhīvati||to spit}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈspiːja/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|iːja|lang=is}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|spjó|spjóu|spúið}} ''or'' {{is-verb-weak|spúði|spúið}}

# to [[vomit]]
# to [[spit]] out, make [[gush]] forth

====Conjugation====
Strong or (increasingly commonly) weak. May also be mixed, with the strong forms being retained mostly in the singular past indicative forms.

===Noun===
{{is-noun|f|spýju|spýjur}}

# [[vomit]]
# a thick [[shower]] of [[rain]] in windy conditions
# a small [[avalanche]]

